        "content":  "PEOPLE\u0027S REPUBLIC OF CHINA\r\n\r\n================================================================\r\nQUICK SUMMARY\r\n================================================================\r\nChina is the world\u0027s second-largest economy and a rising global power challenging US hegemony across trade, technology, and military domains. As a P5 member and the world\u0027s largest manufacturer, it plays a decisive role in几乎所有 international issues.\r\n\r\n================================================================\r\nBASIC INFORMATION\r\n================================================================\r\nCapital: Beijing\r\nLargest City: Shanghai\r\nOfficial Name: People\u0027s Republic of China\r\nGovernment Type: Single-party socialist republic\r\nHead of State: President Xi Jinping\r\nHead of Government: Premier Li Qiang\r\nOfficial Languages: Standard Chinese (Mandarin)\r\nPopulation: ~1.41 billion\r\nArea: 9,596,960 km² (4th largest)\r\nCurrency: Renminbi (CNY)\r\nGDP (Nominal): ~$19.5 trillion (2025)\r\nGDP Per Capita: ~$13,800\r\n\r\n================================================================\r\nECONOMY\r\n================================================================\r\nMajor Industries: Manufacturing, technology, construction, real estate, automotive, electronics, steel, consumer goods\r\nMajor Exports: Broadcasting equipment, computers, integrated circuits, telephones, machinery, textiles\r\nMajor Imports: Crude oil, natural gas, integrated circuits, iron ore, soybeans, machinery, aircraft\r\nMajor Trade Partners: USA, Japan, South Korea, Vietnam, Germany, Australia, Russia, Taiwan\r\n\r\n================================================================\r\nMILITARY \u0026 SECURITY\r\n================================================================\r\nMilitary Overview: Largest active military in the world (~2 million personnel). Rapidly modernizing navy and air force. Major investments in anti-access/area denial (A2/AD) capabilities, hypersonic weapons, and space-based systems.\r\nNuclear Weapons Status: Recognized nuclear weapon state (NPT). ~500 warheads, rapidly expanding arsenal.\r\nUN Membership: Founding member (1945); took ROC seat in 1971\r\nUNSC Status: P5 (permanent member with veto power)\r\nMajor International Organizations: UN, G20, BRICS, SCO, APEC, WTO, Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB)\r\n\r\n================================================================\r\nGEOGRAPHY \u0026 INFLUENCE\r\n================================================================\r\nRegional Influence: Dominant power in East Asia; growing influence in Africa, Middle East, Latin America via Belt and Road Initiative (BRI)\r\nNeighbouring Countries: India, Russia, Mongolia, Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Tajikistan, Afghanistan, Pakistan, Nepal, Bhutan, Myanmar, Laos, Vietnam, North Korea\r\nStrategic Importance: Controls South China Sea trade routes; key player in global supply chains; largest trading partner for 120+ countries\r\nImportant Maritime Routes: South China Sea, East China Sea, Malacca Strait (critical import chokepoint)\r\nImportant Geography: Himalayas (southwest border with India), Taklamakan and Gobi Deserts, Yangtze River economic belt\r\n\r\n================================================================\r\nENERGY \u0026 RESOURCES\r\n================================================================\r\nEnergy Resources: World\u0027s largest coal producer and consumer; largest renewable energy producer (solar, wind, hydro); largest electricity grid globally\r\nNatural Resources: Coal, rare earth elements (dominant global supplier), iron ore, gold, copper, lead, zinc, uranium\r\nTechnology Sector: Rapidly advancing — major AI, 5G, and semiconductor industries (Huawei, Alibaba, Tencent, Baidu, ByteDance, SMIC)\r\nMajor Companies: ICBC, China Construction Bank, Tencent, Alibaba, PetroChina, Sinopec, Huawei, BYD, CATL\r\n\r\n================================================================\r\nSOCIETY\r\n================================================================\r\nEducation Level: High literacy rate (~97%); increasingly high tertiary enrollment\r\nInternet Penetration: ~78% — world\u0027s largest online population\r\nHuman Development Index (HDI): 0.788 (High, ranked 75th)\r\nCorruption Perceptions Index: 42/100 (ranked 65th)\r\nPress Freedom Status: Very restricted — state-controlled media, strict censorship, Great Firewall\r\nHuman Rights Overview: Severe restrictions on political expression, religious freedom (Xinjiang), and digital privacy; mass surveillance via social credit system; concerns over treatment of Uyghurs and Tibetans\r\n\r\n================================================================\r\nFOREIGN POLICY\r\n================================================================\r\nCurrent Leader Priorities: National rejuvenation (Chinese Dream), economic self-sufficiency, technological sovereignty, reunification with Taiwan, countering US influence\r\nForeign Policy Overview: Assertive expansionism — South China Sea claims, Belt and Road infrastructure lending, strategic partnership with Russia, competition with US and India, deepening Africa ties\r\nRelations With:\r\n  USA: Strategic competitor; trade war, technology decoupling, Taiwan tensions\r\n  China: —\r\n  Russia: Strategic partnership; aligned against US hegemony; energy and military cooperation\r\n  India: Border tensions (Doklam, Galwan); strategic rivalry in South Asia and Indian Ocean\r\n  Pakistan: All-weather ally; major infrastructure investment (CPEC); military and nuclear cooperation\r\n  EU: Economic partner but strategic competitor; tensions over human rights, trade imbalances\r\n  Middle East: Growing engagement — energy imports from Gulf, diplomacy with Iran and Saudi Arabia\r\n  Neighbouring Countries: Mixed — dominant economic partner; territorial disputes with India, Vietnam, Philippines\r\n\r\n================================================================\r\nALLIANCES \u0026 RIVALRIES\r\n================================================================\r\nMajor Allies: Pakistan, Russia (strategic partnership), North Korea, Cambodia, Myanmar (junta), Iran (strategic partner)\r\nMajor Rivals: USA, India, Japan, Australia, European Union, NATO\r\n\r\n================================================================\r\nNATIONAL INTERESTS \u0026 CHALLENGES\r\n================================================================\r\nKey National Interests: Economic growth, technological self-sufficiency, energy security, reunification with Taiwan, securing trade routes, countering US influence\r\nCurrent Major Challenges: Economic slowdown and property crisis; demographic decline (aging population); technology sanctions from US; debt trap diplomacy backlash; Xinjiang and Tibet international criticism; tensions over Taiwan\r\n\r\n================================================================\r\nINTERESTING FACTS\r\n================================================================\r\n• China builds more skyscrapers in a year than any other country.\r\n• China controls over 60% of global rare earth element production.\r\n• The South China Sea is the site of disputed island militarization.\r\n• China\u0027s Belt and Road Initiative spans over 140 countries.\r\n\r\n================================================================\r\nSOURCES\r\n================================================================\r\n• CIA World Factbook — China\r\n• World Bank — China Country Data\r\n• IMF — World Economic Outlook Database\r\n• SIPRI — Military Expenditure Database\r\n• UNDP — Human Development Report\r\n• Transparency International — Corruption Perceptions Index\r\n• WTO — Trade Profiles\r\n"
