        "path":  "UNSC/Resources/Statistics.txt",
        "name":  "Statistics.txt",
        "size":  3219,
        "content":  "================================================================\r\nUNSC RESOURCE GUIDE: SHIPPING \u0026 SUPPLY CHAIN STATISTICS | BATTLE CARD\r\n================================================================\r\n\r\n⚡ QUICK REFERENCE\r\n   Committee: UNSC — Agenda: Geopolitical Conflicts, Supply Chains \u0026 Maritime Security\r\n   Power Stats: \"Suez transit down 45%\" / \"Freight rates up 250%\" / \"20.5M barrels/day through Hormuz\"\r\n           \"600+ shadow fleet tankers\" / \"90% of advanced chips from Taiwan\" / \"85% rare earths from China\"\r\n\r\nUse these statistics in the Security Council to quantify the impact of geopolitical conflicts on global trade.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n1. RED SEA \u0026 SUEZ CANAL DISRUPTIONS (2023-2024)\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• Suez Canal Transit Drop: Daily transit volume through the Suez Canal dropped by over 45% following Houthi attacks in the Bab-el-Mandeb.\r\n• Transit Cost Spikes: Rerouting container ships around the Cape of Good Hope (Africa) adds 10-14 days to journey times and increases fuel costs by over $1 million per round trip.\r\n• Global Container Rates: Spot freight rates from Shanghai to Europe increased by over 250% between December 2023 and February 2024.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n2. STRAIT OF HORMUZ ENERGY FLOWS\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• Oil Volume: Approximately 20.5 million barrels of oil per day pass through the Strait of Hormuz (representing 20% of global petroleum consumption).\r\n• LNG Shipments: Over 20% of global liquefied natural gas (LNG) shipments transit through Hormuz, primarily sourced from Qatar.\r\n• Choke Point Dependency: Over 75% of crude oil transiting Hormuz is destined for Asian markets (China, India, Japan, South Korea).\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n3. THE RUSSIAN SHADOW FLEET\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• Tanker Count: Estimates indicate the Russian shadow fleet consists of over 600 aging tankers (many older than 15 years, nearing decommissioning).\r\n• Insurance Deficit: Over 90% of these vessels operate without verified Protection and Indemnity (P\u0026I) insurance from major Western clubs.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n4. SEMICONDUCTOR \u0026 RAW MATERIAL CONCENTRATIONS\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• Advanced Chips: Over 90% of the world\u0027s most advanced semiconductors (under 10nm) are manufactured in Taiwan, highlighting the supply chain risk of regional conflict.\r\n• Rare Earth Elements: China processes over 85% of global rare earth elements, critical for electric vehicles and defense systems.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\nOFFICIAL SOURCES\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• UNCTAD Maritime Transport Review\r\n• International Energy Agency (IEA) Energy Statistics\r\n• World Bank Food Security and Trade Bulletins\r\n• Lloyd\u0027s List Intelligence Reports\r\n================================================================\r\n"
