        "content":  "================================================================\r\nUNSC RESOURCE GUIDE: USEFUL SOURCES \u0026 TRADE WATCHDOGS | BATTLE CARD\r\n================================================================\r\n\r\n⚡ QUICK REFERENCE\r\n   Committee: UNSC — Agenda: Geopolitical Conflicts, Supply Chains \u0026 Maritime Security\r\n   Quick Cites: IMO (maritime law) / UNCTAD (trade data) / WTO (disputes) / Lloyd\u0027s List (ship tracking)\r\n           ICC IMB (piracy incidents) / IEA (energy markets) / World Bank (food security)\r\n\r\nThis document lists the most reliable organizations and databases to monitor for real-time shipping and trade data during committee.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n1. INTERGOVERNMENTAL MARITIME BODIES\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• International Maritime Organization (IMO):\r\n  - Website: https://www.imo.org\r\n  - Focus: The specialized UN agency responsible for the safety and security of shipping and prevention of marine pollution.\r\n• UN Conference on Trade and Development (UNCTAD):\r\n  - Website: https://unctad.org\r\n  - Focus: Publishes the annual Review of Maritime Transport, the definitive statistical analysis on global fleet sizes, container volumes, and transit costs.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n2. TRADE \u0026 ECONOMIC WATCHDOGS\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• World Trade Organization (WTO):\r\n  - Website: https://www.wto.org\r\n  - Focus: Tracks global trade disputes, tariff changes, and trade restrictive measures under national security exceptions.\r\n• World Bank Group - Global Trade Portal:\r\n  - Website: https://www.worldbank.org\r\n  - Focus: Tracks food security indices, fertilizer supply chains, and infrastructure development loans.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n3. INDUSTRY INTELLIGENCE \u0026 RESEARCH ORGS\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• Lloyd\u0027s List Intelligence:\r\n  - Website: https://lloydslistintelligence.com\r\n  - Focus: Provides real-time tracking of merchant shipping, vessel registrations, insurance status, and port delays.\r\n• ICC International Maritime Bureau (IMB):\r\n  - Website: https://www.icc-ccs.org/icc/imb\r\n  - Focus: Tracks global piracy incidents and acts of armed robbery against ships in real-time.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\nOFFICIAL SOURCES\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• United Nations General Assembly Maritime Affairs Database\r\n• International Energy Agency (IEA) Oil Market Reports\r\n================================================================\r\n"
