        "path":  "UNSC/Resources/WTO.txt",
        "name":  "WTO.txt",
        "size":  3035,
        "content":  "================================================================\r\nUNSC RESOURCE GUIDE: WTO RULES \u0026 NATIONAL SECURITY EXCEPTIONS | BATTLE CARD\r\n================================================================\r\n\r\n⚡ QUICK REFERENCE\r\n   Committee: UNSC — Agenda: Geopolitical Conflicts, Supply Chains \u0026 Maritime Security\r\n   Key Articles: GATT Art XXI — Security exceptions (used to justify sanctions/export controls)\r\n           GATT Art V — Freedom of transit / GATT Art I — Most-Favored-Nation treatment\r\n           Art XXI is YOUR battleground — is it legitimate security or protectionism?\r\n\r\nThis document reviews the primary articles of the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT/WTO) relevant to trade blocks, tariffs, and supply chain security.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n1. GATT ARTICLE XXI - SECURITY EXCEPTIONS\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• Summary: Permits member states to take any action they consider necessary for the protection of their essential security interests:\r\n  - Relating to fissionable materials.\r\n  - Relating to traffic in arms, ammunition, and implements of war.\r\n  - Taken in time of war or other emergency in international relations.\r\n• Debate Application:\r\n  - Cited by the US and partners to justify semiconductor export bans and tariffs on strategic materials (EVs, minerals) from China.\r\n  - Opposing states argue that Article XXI is being abused as a protectionist tool to disrupt legitimate commercial supply chains.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n2. GATT ARTICLE V - FREEDOM OF TRANSIT\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• Summary: Mandates freedom of transit through the territory of each member for traffic in transit to or from the territory of other members.\r\n• Key Constraint:\r\n  - Prohibits discrimination based on flag of vessel, origin, departure, entry, or destination of goods.\r\n• Debate Application:\r\n  - Cited when challenging border blockades, transport routing bans, or pipeline closures enacted by states during conflicts.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n3. GATT ARTICLE I - MOST-FAVORED-NATION (MFN) TREATMENT\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• Summary: Requires that any advantage, favor, or privilege granted to a product from one member state must be extended immediately and unconditionally to all other WTO members.\r\n• Debate Application:\r\n  - \"Friend-shoring\" policies that offer lower tariffs or regulatory ease exclusively to allied states represent a direct violation of MFN treatment, unless justified under Article XXI.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\nOFFICIAL SOURCES\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• World Trade Organization (WTO) Legal Texts\r\n• GATT 1994 Treaty Documents\r\n================================================================\r\n"
