        "content":  "================================================================\r\nUNSC MODERATED CAUCUS TALKING POINTS | BATTLE CARD\r\n================================================================\r\n\r\n⚡ QUICK REFERENCE\r\n   Agenda: Impact of Geopolitical Conflicts on Global Supply Chains, Maritime Security \u0026 Free Trade\r\n   Use Case: Motion passes → Pick your topic → Grab pro/con arguments → 30-45 sec speech\r\n   Key Motion Examples: \"Red Sea coalition patrols\" / \"Shadow fleet regulation\" / \"Undersea cable protection\"\r\n\r\nUse these modular talking points to quickly prepare speeches for specific moderated caucuses in the Security Council.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\nTOPIC 1: RED SEA MARITIME SAFETY \u0026 COALITION patrols\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\nSuggested Motion: \"Motion for a moderated caucus of 10 minutes with a 30-second speaking time on the deployment of defensive coalitions in the Red Sea.\"\r\n\r\nWESTERN MARITIME BLOC ARGUMENTS:\r\n• Houthi missile and drone attacks on merchant shipping violate international law and represent an act of regional terrorism.\r\n• Operations like Prosperity Guardian are purely defensive, necessary to protect civilian lives and keep global trade lanes open.\r\n• The UNSC must coordinate targeted interdictions to halt the illicit flow of weapons to proxy groups.\r\n\r\nSOVEREIGN BLOC ARGUMENTS:\r\n• Western-led military coalitions in the Red Sea escalate regional conflicts and fail to address the root political causes.\r\n• These patrols represent a unilateral attempt to establish naval hegemony in a strategic transit zone without UN authorization.\r\n• True security can only be achieved through regional dialogue and respect for the territorial waters of coastal states.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\nTOPIC 2: REGULATING THE RUSSIAN SHADOW FLEET\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\nSuggested Motion: \"Motion for a moderated caucus of 12 minutes with a 45-second speaking time on the security risks of the shadow fleet.\"\r\n\r\nSANCTIONS-ENFORCING BLOC ARGUMENTS:\r\n• The Russian shadow fleet of older, un-insured, and poorly maintained tankers presents an imminent environmental risk of oil spills in busy transit zones.\r\n• These vessels bypass G7 oil price caps using flags of convenience, undermining the rule of law and international accountability.\r\n• We call on coastal states to deny transit access to tankers lacking verified commercial P\u0026I insurance.\r\n\r\nANTI-SANCTIONS BLOC ARGUMENTS:\r\n• Unilateral Western sanctions are the direct cause of the shift in shipping logistics and are illegal under WTO rules.\r\n• Attempts to block Russian agricultural and energy exports threaten global energy stability and cause inflation in developing nations.\r\n• Commercial operators have the right to select flags of convenience and insurance pools free from political coercion.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\nTOPIC 3: DEFENDING UNDERSEA CRITICAL INFRASTRUCTURE\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\nSuggested Motion: \"Motion for a moderated caucus of 15 minutes with a 45-second speaking time on protecting undersea cables and energy pipelines.\"\r\n\r\nCOOPERATIVE SECURITY ARGUMENTS:\r\n• Undersea communication cables carry 95% of global internet traffic. Sabotage of these networks would cause global financial collapse.\r\n• We call for a UN-led Undersea Cable Sentinel Network to share real-time sonar and satellite data on suspicious maritime vessel movements.\r\n• Sovereign states must coordinate cybersecurity and physical defense protocols for critical energy pipelines in international waters.\r\n\r\nSOVEREIGN BLOC ARGUMENTS:\r\n• Infrastructure security remains the sole responsibility of the coastal state within its EEZ and territorial waters.\r\n• We reject attempts by foreign military alliances to police our undersea assets under the guise of cooperative security.\r\n• Independent, transparent UN-led investigations are needed to identify the state actors behind the Nord Stream pipeline sabotage.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\nOFFICIAL SOURCES\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n• International Maritime Organization (IMO) Safety Committee\r\n• UN Conference on Trade and Development (UNCTAD) Maritime Transport Review\r\n================================================================\r\n"
